es are available to members. For information about board meetings or to get involved, please contact us.","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"md","textColor":"default"}}]},{"type":"section","bg":"light","padding":"md","children":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Bylaws & Governance","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"lg","textColor":"default"}},{"type":"text","body":"NRCGA operates under established bylaws that govern our organization''s structure, membership, and decision-making processes. These bylaws ensure transparency, accountability, and effective governance of our alliance.","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"md","textColor":"default"}},{"type":"cta_button","label":"View Bylaws & Standing Rules","url":"bylaws.html","style":{"align":"left"}},{"type":"text","body":"For information about meeting minutes or other governance documents, please contact us.","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"md","textColor":"default"}}]},{"type":"section","bg":"default","padding":"md","children":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Common Ground Alliance","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"lg","textColor":"default"}},{"type":"text","body":"NRCGA is a regional partner of the national Common Ground Alliance.","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"md","textColor":"default"}},{"type":"text","body":"The Common Ground Alliance (CGA) is the national organization dedicated to preventing damage to underground utility infrastructure and protecting those who live and work near these important assets. CGA provides a forum where stakeholders can share information and perspectives and work together on all aspects of damage prevention issues.","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"md","textColor":"default"}},{"type":"text","body":"As a regional partner, NRCGA aligns with CGA''s mission and best practices while addressing the specific needs of Nevada''s damage prevention community. We work together to promote safety, share knowledge, and advance damage prevention initiatives at both the regional and national levels.","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"md","textColor":"default"}},{"type":"cta_button","label":"Visit Common Ground Alliance","url":"http://commongroundalliance.com/","style":{"align":"left"}}]},{"type":"section","bg":"light","padding":"md","children":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Public Utilities Commission of Nevada","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"lg","textColor":"default"}},{"type":"text","body":"NRCGA works closely with the Public Utilities Commission of Nevada to promote damage prevention.","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"md","textColor":"default"}},{"type":"text","body":"The Public Utilities Commission of Nevada (PUCN) is the state regulatory agency responsible for overseeing utilities and ensuring public safety. The PUCN plays a vital role in damage prevention by regulating utility operations and enforcing excavation safety requirements in Nevada.","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"md","textColor":"default"}},{"type":"text","body":"NRCGA collaborates with the PUCN to support damage prevention initiatives, provide education and training, and ensure that Nevada''s excavation laws and regulations are effectively implemented. The PUCN also hosts NRCGA membership meetings at their offices in both Carson City and Las Vegas, facilitating statewide participation in damage prevention efforts.","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"md","textColor":"default"}},{"type":"cta_button","label":"Visit PUCN Website","url":"https://puc.nv.gov/","style":{"align":"left"}}]},{"type":"section","bg":"default","padding":"md","children":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Join NRCGA","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"lg","textColor":"default"}},{"type":"text","body":"Become part of Nevada''s damage prevention community and help us build a safer state.","style":{"align":"left","textSize":"md","textColor":"default"}},{"type":"cta_button","label":"Get Involved","url":"contact.html","style":{"align":"left"}}]}]', '<section class="content-section">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="content-grid">
                <div class="content-text">
                    <h2>Our Mission</h2>
                    <p>
                        NRCGA is dedicated to promoting public safety and damage prevention across Nevada. We bring together
                        excavators, utility operators, locators, and stakeholders to build a culture of safety through
                        education, collaboration, and continuous improvement.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Every dig matters. Every call to 811 prevents potential damage, protects lives, and ensures the
                        reliability of essential services. We''re committed to building a safer Nevada where underground
                        infrastructure is protected and respected.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="content-visual">
                    <img src="assets/images/programs/nrcga-meeting.jpg" alt="NRCGA members collaborating" style="width: 100%; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: var(--shadow-md); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;" onerror="this.style.display=''none''">
                    <div class="visual-card">
                        <h3>Our Impact</h3>
                        <ul class="impact-list">
                            <li>Education &amp; Training Programs</li>
                            <li>Damage Prevention Initiatives</li>
                            <li>Community Outreach</li>
                            <li>Industry Collaboration</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section bg-light">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">What We Do</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">NRCGA supports Nevada''s damage prevention community through multiple programs and initiatives.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="features-grid">
                <div class="feature-item">
                    <div class="feature-icon">🎓</div>
                    <h3>Education &amp; Training</h3>
                    <p>Comprehensive safety training programs for excavators, locators, and utility operators across Northern and Southern Nevada.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-item">
                    <div class="feature-icon">🤝</div>
                    <h3>Industry Collaboration</h3>
                    <p>Bringing together stakeholders from across the damage prevention industry to share best practices and improve processes.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-item">
                    <div class="feature-icon">📊</div>
                    <h3>Data &amp; Reporting</h3>
                    <p>Tracking damage incidents through DIRT (Damage Information Reporting Tool) to identify trends and improve prevention.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-item">
                    <div class="feature-icon">🏆</div>
                    <h3>Recognition Programs</h3>
                    <p>Celebrating excellence through awards like the Silver Shovel Awards and Zero At-Fault Damages recognition.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-item">
                    <div class="feature-icon">📅</div>
                    <h3>Events &amp; Outreach</h3>
                    <p>Organizing events like 811 Day, Utility Locate Rodeo, and community outreach to raise awareness.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="feature-item">
                    <div class="feature-icon">💬</div>
                    <h3>Advocacy</h3>
                    <p>Advocating for policies and practices that promote safety and protect Nevada''s underground infrastructure.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section style="position: relative; height: 50vh; min-height: 350px; background-image: url(''assets/images/programs/home/ExcavationDiabloDr2025.resized.jpg''); background-size: 120% auto; background-position: center; background-attachment: fixed; background-repeat: no-repeat;">
        <div style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">Board &amp; Leadership</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">NRCGA is governed by a board of directors representing various stakeholders in Nevada''s damage prevention community.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="board-info">
                <p>
                    Our board members represent excavators, utility operators, locators, and other key stakeholders.
                    They volunteer their time and expertise to guide NRCGA''s mission and programs.
                </p>
                <div style="text-align: center; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                    <a href="members.html" class="btn btn-primary">View Board of Directors &amp; Members</a>
                </div>
                <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                    Board meetings are held regularly, and minutes are available to members. For information about
                    board meetings or to get involved, please <a href="contact.html">contact us</a>.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section bg-light">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">Bylaws &amp; Governance</h2>
            </div>

            <div class="content-text">
                <p>
                    NRCGA operates under established bylaws that govern our organization''s structure, membership,
                    and decision-making processes. These bylaws ensure transparency, accountability, and effective
                    governance of our alliance.
                </p>
                <div style="margin-top: 2rem; display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center;">
                    <a href="bylaws.html" class="btn btn-primary">View Bylaws &amp; Standing Rules</a>
                </div>
                <p style="margin-top: 2rem;">
                    For information about meeting minutes or other governance documents, please
                    <a href="contact.html">contact us</a>.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">Common Ground Alliance</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">NRCGA is a regional partner of the national Common Ground Alliance.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="content-text" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
                <p>
                    The <a href="http://commongroundalliance.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Common Ground Alliance (CGA)</a>
                    is the national organization dedicated to preventing damage to underground utility infrastructure and protecting those who
                    live and work near these important assets. CGA provides a forum where stakeholders can share information and perspectives
                    and work together on all aspects of damage prevention issues.
                </p>
                <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                    As a regional partner, NRCGA aligns with CGA''s mission and best practices while addressing the specific needs of Nevada''s
                    damage prevention community. We work together to promote safety, share knowledge, and advance damage prevention initiatives
                    at both the regional and national levels.
                </p>
                <div style="margin-top: 2rem; text-align: center;">
                    <a href="http://commongroundalliance.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary">Visit Common Ground Alliance</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section bg-light">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="section-header">
                <h2 class="section-title">Public Utilities Commission of Nevada</h2>
                <p class="section-subtitle">NRCGA works closely with the Public Utilities Commission of Nevada to promote damage prevention.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="content-text" style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
                <p>
                    The <a href="https://puc.nv.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Public Utilities Commission of Nevada (PUCN)</a>
                    is the state regulatory agency responsible for overseeing utilities and ensuring public safety. The PUCN plays a vital role in
                    damage prevention by regulating utility operations and enforcing excavation safety requirements in Nevada.
                </p>
                <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
                    NRCGA collaborates with the PUCN to support damage prevention initiatives, provide education and training, and ensure that
                    Nevada''s excavation laws and regulations are effectively implemented. The PUCN also hosts NRCGA membership meetings at their
                    offices in both Carson City and Las Vegas, facilitating statewide participation in damage prevention efforts.
                </p>
                <div style="margin-top: 2rem; text-align: center;">
                    <a href="https://puc.nv.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary">Visit PUCN Website</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cta-section">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="cta-content">
                <h2>Join NRCGA</h2>
                <p>Become part of Nevada''s damage prevention community and help us build a safer state.</p>
                <a href="contact.html" class="btn btn-primary">Get Involved</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>', NULL, 1, 0);